you to three new features.

00:13:53.590 --> 00:14:00.140
So the first place,
custom images,

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:02.900
so our base Dataproc images
come with four components,

00:14:02.900 --> 00:14:04.880
Hadoop, Spark, Hive, and Pig.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.434
But oftentimes you want
to run more than that.

00:14:07.434 --> 00:14:09.350
Sometimes you can bring
your Java dependencies

00:14:09.350 --> 00:14:10.020
with your job.

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:12.285
But oftentimes you need
to bring a lot more.

00:14:12.285 --> 00:14:13.910
So if you installing
servers, or you're

00:14:13.910 --> 00:14:16.400
compiling Python
dependencies from source,

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:17.820
that can take a lot longer.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:19.370
So once your
initialization actions

00:14:19.370 --> 00:14:21.390
take more than
just a few minutes,

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:23.199
now if you create
a large cluster,

00:14:23.199 --> 00:14:24.740
either your [INAUDIBLE]
actions, I've

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:26.545
even heard a customer
take an hour.

00:14:26.545 --> 00:14:27.920
Now you're spending
all that time

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:29.294
just configuring
the cluster, not

00:14:29.294 --> 00:14:30.770
actually processing the data.

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:33.770
So the custom image,
you can build an image

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:36.424
and then give that to Dataproc
to use for your clusters.

00:14:36.424 --> 00:14:38.465
And that really helps you
use ephemeral clusters.

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:44.280
So I'm going to just
